  "hindi": "हे मित्र और वरुण, हमारे रथ की रक्षा करो, जो आदित्यों, रुद्रों और वसुओं के साथ सहचर है; जब वे पक्षियों के समान निवास से उड़ चले, यश चाहनेवाले, उत्साहित, वन में बैठनेवाले।",
  "english": "O Mitra and Varuṇa, protect our chariot, being together with the Ādityas, Rudras and Vasus; when they flew forth like birds from the dwelling, desiring fame, eager, sitting in the wood.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "'sacābhuvā' is taken as an instrumental 'being together (with)'; its exact sense and what it qualifies is uncertain. 'vasmanaḥ pari' rendered 'from the dwelling' (vasman uncertain). The referent of the plural 'they' in the second line (śravasyavaḥ hṛṣīvantaḥ vanarṣadaḥ) is not stated; the Ādityas, Rudras and Vasus are not certain. 'śravasyavaḥ' also 'desiring glory/food'. 'vanarṣadaḥ' could also mean 'sitting in wood' (chariot).",
  "confidence": "low",
  "type": "verse",
  "line_ids": [
   "002.031.1a",
   "002.031.1b"
  ],
  "lines_deva": [
   "अ॒स्माकं॑ मित्रावरुणावतं॒ रथ॑मादि॒त्यै रु॒द्रैर्वसु॑भिः सचा॒भुवा॑",
   "प्र यद् वयो॒ न पप्त॒न्वस्म॑न॒स्परि॑ श्रव॒स्यवो॒ हृषी॑वन्तो वन॒र्षद॑:"
