  "hindi": "अब, हे एकमत देवो, हमारे रथ की, जो जनों के बीच पुरस्कार चाहता है, सहायता करो, जब वे तेज चलनेवाले अपने पैरों से धूल को पार करते हुए पृथ्वी की सतह पर हाथों से बार-बार प्रहार करते हैं।",
  "english": "Now, O gods of one accord, help our chariot that seeks the prize among the clans, when the swift ones, crossing the dust with their feet, strike again and again on the surface of the earth with their hands.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "'titrataḥ' is of uncertain form and sense (taken as a participle 'crossing'); 'rajaḥ' could be 'dust' or 'space'. 'pāṇibhiḥ' is literally 'hands' (for the swift ones' forefeet); not interpreted. 'udavata' taken as ud-√av, 'help'. 'sma' is the particle with adha. 'naḥ' taken as 'our' with ratham.",
  "confidence": "low",
  "type": "verse",
