  "hindi": "और वह हमारा इन्द्र, सब जनों का, उत्तम संकल्पवाला, आकाश के मरुतों के दल के साथ, सुरक्षित सहायताओं से हमारे रथ का अब साथ दे, बड़े लाभ के लिए, पुरस्कार जीतने के लिए।",
  "english": "And that Indra of ours, of all peoples, of good resolve, with the troop of the Maruts of the sky, may now attend our chariot with safe helps, for great gain, for the winning of the prize.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "'divaḥ' is taken with the Maruts ('of the sky'); it might go with Indra. 'viśvacarṣaṇi' taken as 'of all peoples' (also 'all-seeing'). 'avṛkābhiḥ' literally 'not wolfish', rendered 'safe'. 'ūtibhī ratham' is ūtibhiḥ ratham (visarga lost before r). The sense 'attend' for anu-√sthā is the drafter's choice.",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "type": "verse",
  "line_ids": [
   "002.031.3a",
   "002.031.3b"
  ],
  "lines_deva": [
   "उ॒त स्य न॒ इन्द्रो॑ वि॒श्वच॑र्षणिर्दि॒वः शर्धे॑न॒ मारु॑तेन सु॒क्रतु॑:",
   "अनु॒ नु स्था॑त्यवृ॒काभि॑रू॒तिभी॒ रथं॑ म॒हे स॒नये॒ वाज॑सातये"
  ],
